WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.165
Nothing to fear.

00:01.910 --> 00:06.554
The Sun will never be a black hole: only stars many times heavier end that way.

00:07.046 --> 00:12.177
And if you swapped the Sun for a black hole of the same mass, the planets would stay in their orbits.

00:12.694 --> 00:14.249
It would only get a lot colder.

00:14.834 --> 00:18.808
The nearest black hole we know is about fifteen hundred light-years away.
